.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/@isaacs/cliui Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "@isaacs/cliui"
.PP
Temporary fork of \fRcliui\fP\&.

.PP
 \fR\fP \fR\fP 

.PP
easily create complex multi-column command-line-interfaces\&.
.SH "Example"
.PP
.PP
.nf
const ui = require('cliui')()

ui\&.div('Usage: $0 [command] [options]')

ui\&.div({
  text: 'Options:',
  padding: [2, 0, 1, 0]
})

ui\&.div(
  {
    text: "\-f, \-\-file",
    width: 20,
    padding: [0, 4, 0, 4]
  },
  {
    text: "the file to load\&." +
      chalk\&.green("(if this description is long it wraps)\&.")
    ,
    width: 20
  },
  {
    text: chalk\&.red("[required]"),
    align: 'right'
  }
)

console\&.log(ui\&.toString())
.fi
.PP
.SH "Deno/ESM Support"
.PP
As of \fRv7\fP \fRcliui\fP supports \fRDeno\fP and \fRESM\fP:

.PP
.PP
.nf
import cliui from "https://deno\&.land/x/cliui/deno\&.ts";

const ui = cliui({})

ui\&.div('Usage: $0 [command] [options]')

ui\&.div({
  text: 'Options:',
  padding: [2, 0, 1, 0]
})

ui\&.div({
  text: "\-f, \-\-file",
  width: 20,
  padding: [0, 4, 0, 4]
})

console\&.log(ui\&.toString())
.fi
.PP

.PP
.SH "Layout DSL"
.PP
cliui exposes a simple layout DSL:

.PP
If you create a single \fRui\&.div\fP, passing a string rather than an object:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR\\n\fP: characters will be interpreted as new rows\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR\\t\fP: characters will be interpreted as new columns\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR\\s\fP: characters will be interpreted as padding\&.
.PP

.PP
\fBas an example\&.\&.\&.\fP

.PP
.PP
.nf
var ui = require('\&./')({
  width: 60
})

ui\&.div(
  'Usage: node \&./bin/foo\&.js\\n' +
  '  <regex>\\t  provide a regex\\n' +
  '  <glob>\\t  provide a glob\\t [required]'
)

console\&.log(ui\&.toString())
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBwill output:\fP

.PP
.PP
.nf
Usage: node \&./bin/foo\&.js
  <regex>  provide a regex
  <glob>   provide a glob          [required]
.fi
.PP
.SH "Methods"
.PP
.PP
.nf
cliui = require('cliui')
.fi
.PP
.SS "cliui({width: integer})"
Specify the maximum width of the UI being generated\&. If no width is provided, cliui will try to get the current window's width and use it, and if that doesn't work, width will be set to \fR80\fP\&.
.SS "cliui({wrap: boolean})"
Enable or disable the wrapping of text in a column\&.
.SS "cliui\&.div(column, column, column)"
Create a row with any number of columns, a column can either be a string, or an object with the following options:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBtext:\fP some text to place in the column\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBwidth:\fP the width of a column\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBalign:\fP alignment, \fRright\fP or \fRcenter\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBpadding:\fP \fR[top, right, bottom, left]\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBborder:\fP should a border be placed around the div?
.PP
.SS "cliui\&.span(column, column, column)"
Similar to \fRdiv\fP, except the next row will be appended without a new line being created\&.
.SS "cliui\&.resetOutput()"
Resets the UI elements of the current cliui instance, maintaining the values set for \fRwidth\fP and \fRwrap\fP\&. 
